  "command": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_DOTNET_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_DOTNET='/app/.toolchains/dotnet/dotnet' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_DOTNET_ROUTES='ordinary' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_DOTNET_MODES='full' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_DOTNET_OUTPUT='build/vo1444-nominal-dotnet-ordinary-full-r2-5762111-records' LEAN_BRIDGE_LEAN_PREFIX='/app/.toolchains/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.32.2' LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_TEST_GLIBC_FLOOR='2.36' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE='1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' '/usr/bin/nice' '-n' '19' '/usr/bin/ionice' '-c' '3' '/usr/bin/taskset' '-c' '3' '/usr/bin/node' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' 'tests/helpers/nominal-subtype-dotnet-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author roots reproduce the complete NuGet package. Author sources are removed before offline installation; unchanged callers replay after moving each installed consumer tree and again after deleting all consumer sources, for three executions per selection. The full fixture checks per-use constructor selection and normalization, repeated record fields, active variant branches, aliases, mixed Fin guards, exact rejection paths, caller-input preservation and recovery. Nominal acceptance covers the tested Nat Subtype records, variants, aliases and copied constructor-free results with .NET SDK 8.0.424 and shared framework 8.0.30 through offline NuGet installation on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor. Consumers run after relocation and again after removal of all consumer sources. Other primitive-base nominal fixtures and other hosts need separate acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain pending. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured; these local runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance. The repository archive omits package binaries and full toolchains; receipts, installed-file hashes and selected source snapshots are retained. The complete SDK and shared framework remain trusted tools.",
